VideoBanana and ChatVE-Bench

The code in this repository is released under the Apache License 2.0 (LICENSE), except for the parts
listed below, which keep the license of their source.

The checklist judge in chatve_bench/ (the system prompts in chatve_bench/prompts/, the request format, the answer
parsing, and the scoring rules in chatve_bench/judge.py) is adapted from the CoinVE-Bench evaluator,
https://huggingface.co/datasets/FireCRT/CoinVE-Bench, licensed under CC BY-SA 4.0
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/). These adapted parts are shared under the same license.

The rubric of the VideoBanana verifier prompt (VERIFIER_SYSTEM in videobanana/conversation/verifier.py: the three
dimensions, their criteria, scoring rubrics and notes) is adapted from the VEFX-Bench reward prompt,
https://github.com/Visko-Platform/VEFX-Bench, licensed under the Apache License 2.0
(https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0). Changes: the intents are passed in the request and instruction
following is scored per intent, a survey step and an explanations section are added, and the multi-turn verifier
rewrites the lines that take Video 1 to be the unedited source.
